/* Deep lessons — Recursion va backtracking (backtracking).
 *
 * The section where the machine has to become visible. A learner who cannot
 * picture the call stack will not trust a recursive function, and one who
 * cannot picture the search tree will not see why a single early check deletes
 * a million states.
 *
 * So this track draws what is normally invisible: frames piling up and
 * unwinding, a branch being abandoned mid-descent, the squares a queen
 * forbids, the bits standing in for a subset. Nothing here asks the reader to
 * "just believe" that recursion works.
 *
 * Original text and diagrams. Nothing copied from any source.
 */

